From: "omharde@4" <you@example.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 11:13:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] fix(auth): eliminate OAuth open redirects and token
 leakage in URLs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- googleRedirect derived the redirect target from the Origin/Referer header,
  both attacker-controlled, enabling an open redirect (reflected unvalidated
  redirect). The target is now config.frontendUrl only.
- Steam/Discord callback URLs are built from config.apiUrl instead of the Host
  header (Host-header injection -> open redirect / flow hijack).
- OAuth access/refresh tokens were appended to the redirect URL query string,
  leaking into server access logs, browser history and Referer headers. They
  now travel in the URL fragment (#accessToken=...), which is never sent to
  servers. The web callback page reads the fragment first, with the legacy
  query-string path kept for backward compatibility.

Validation: cd server && npx tsc --noEmit; cd web && npx tsc --noEmit.

